                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I am not sure what the deal is with the hate for a $1 game. It is a lot of fun, and for a buck, I was pleasantly surprised. I wish it had more levels as the 2 it has get old after a while. It also says that you do not need the left controller, but found that the Menu button on the Rift's left controller acts as a camera reset as well (expect the Vive is the same)\n\nI am not huge into TD games, but the cute voxel version is kind of like playing with a play set. You also have the option to go onto the Ground Level and watch things occur from the gameboard instead of the elevated level. I recommend the Tutorial first as I had a problem understanding some of the weaponry, but the Flamethrower is sweet!\n\nI also wish that it had an easier way to adjust the game board as I had to look through the Options Menu (which has some sweet options) to find an adjustment so I could sit down instead of stand around. \n\nI recommend the game, it is a dollar, it is fun, and you can go Gangsta with teh blue handgun .",
